      "title": "APTPUO - Winter 2027 - ESL4011-A",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location: Main Campus Academic Period: 2027 Winter Semester Faculty: Faculté des arts / Faculty of Arts Academic Unit: Institut des langues officielles et du bilinguisme \\\\ Official Languages and Bilingualism Institute (OLBI) Course Title: Academic Writing for Publication Course Code: ESL 4011 Section: A Course Description: This hybrid academic writing workshop series is designed for non-Anglophone professors and academic staff who would like to develop and improve their writing skills to effectively write and publish academic work in English. There will be three group workshops during which participants will discuss the following topics: • Refence material and resources for academic work • Principles of grammar, style and vocabulary development • Typical text models and manuscript analysis 3 group meetings (Thursday): February 4, March 4 and April 1, 2027 from 3:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m. Please note that this course is given online (virtual mode). Posting limited to: Instructeur de langue à temps partiel (ILOB) / Part-Time Language Instructor (OLBI) Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/01 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/11/01 Expected Enrolment: 10 Approval date: 2026/10/01 Number of credits: 0 Work Hours: 6 Hourly Rate: ILOB - Cours de langue au personnel / OLBI - Personnel Language Courses: $115.43 (2024-2025) The academic year starts on September 1 and ends on August 31. These rates do not included vacation pay nor statutory pay. These rates will be applied until a new collective agreement is ratified. Retro will be paid after the ratification. Course type: D Posting type: Irrégulier / Irregular Language of instruction: Anglais | English Competence in second language: N/A Course Schedule: Jeudi | Thursday 15:00-17:00 - - 3 group meetings (Thursday): February 4, March 4 and April 1, 2027 3:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m. Requirements: B.A. with specialization in a field rel