      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location: Main Campus Academic Period: 2027 Winter Semester Faculty: Faculté des sciences sociales / Faculty of Social Sciences Academic Unit: École de psychologie \\\\ School of Psychology Course Title: Child Psychopathology Course Code: PSY6132 Section: A00 Course Description: Patterns of child development and childhood psychopathology. Study of specific psychopathological conditions and implications for appropriate treatment. Posting limited to: Professeur à temps-partiel régulier / Regular Part-Time Professor Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/10/13 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2027/11/13 Expected Enrolment: 20 Approval date: 2026/10/13 Number of credits: 3 Work Hours: 39 Hourly Rate: Enseignement / Teaching: $239.47 (2024-2025) The academic year starts on September 1 and ends on August 31. These rates do not included vacation pay nor statutory pay. These rates will be applied until a new collective agreement is ratified. Retro will be paid after the ratification. Course type: C Posting type: Régulier / Regular Language of instruction: Anglais | English Competence in second language: Passive Course Schedule: Lundi | Monday 11:30-14:30 - - This course is offered in person. Requirements: Doctorate in professional psychology (APA or CPA accredited program) Registered with the College of Psychologists of Ontario to provide clinical psychology services to adults Comprehensive knowledge of and evidence of scholarship in psychopathology Comprehensive knowledge of DSM-5 and ICD-11 diagnostic systems Extensive experience in assessing children and adolescents with a range of mental disorders Experienced in administration of Structured Clinical Interview for DSM Disorders Demonstrated  competency incorporating equity, diversity, and inclusion principles in teaching and/or training (formal training in anti-racist, anti-discriminatory, anti-oppressive,  and inclusive practic